  "text": "The manuscript and ending for this telling. This version is recorded after Sol finishes sharing.\n\nI couldn't check that response reliably. You can reread Mara's explanation or continue planning.\n\nThe tape crosses the tear and holds the wing. Let the boy carry his repaired bird onto the dock.\n\nThis is the flower Pip and Grandma grew. After Grandma shares her story, choose a memory for it.\n\nKnown local/source allocations and both instance-matrix copies; not total browser or GPU memory\n\nSol shared A Small Repair with your suggested ending. The added wording is your interpretation.\n\nChoose a picture. Arrow keys move it; Enter places it. Escape returns it to its previous place.\n\nSol brought his manuscript to the garden. Mara crossed the footbridge after finishing her work.\n\nMara reached toward the bird, but the boy pulled it closer. Ask him whether he would like help.\n\nInstall the posts, then draw each rope to the next post. The two sides are fastened separately.\n\nChoose the words that show why the repair mattered. Try reading those words with more emphasis.\n\nRead your whole story aloud while Loop changes the pictures. Pause whenever you need more time.\n\nMove the selected section, then press Enter or choose Place section. Escape cancels this move.\n\nMara helps the last passengers safely ashore. Her work finishes when everyone is off the boat.\n\nShe came all the way to your workshop with the loaf. I’m glad you kept that part in the story.\n\nSol says: “That gives me something to add when I work on the ending. Thank you for listening.”\n\nThe rock blocks that way. The seed is safe aboard. Drag around it or turn with the arrow keys.\n\nGPU elapsed time for submitted rendering; nonblocking; excludes presentation and input latency",
